          <fr:mainmatter>
            <fr:p>I am a mathematician and computer scientist. My <fr:link type="local" href="dhsorens-phd.xml" addr="dhsorens-phd" title="PhD in Formal Methods">PhD</fr:link> was in formal specification of smart contracts in Coq, focusing on the problem of ensuring that specifications actually reflect the high-level intentions of their designers. Formal proposition and proof catch my attention in computer science, from various angles. These days, I am mostly interested in <fr:link type="local" href="dhsorens-lean.xml" addr="dhsorens-lean" title="The Lean Theorem Prover">Lean</fr:link>.</fr:p>
            <fr:p>Here you can see my <fr:link type="local" href="dhsorens-rsrch.xml" addr="dhsorens-rsrch" title="Research">research</fr:link>, <fr:link type="local" href="dhsorens-notes.xml" addr="dhsorens-notes" title="Notes">notes</fr:link>, <fr:link type="local" href="dhsorens-001C.xml" addr="dhsorens-001C" title="Work Bio">work history</fr:link>, and <fr:link type="local" href="dhsorens.xml" addr="dhsorens" title="Derek Sorensen">bio</fr:link>.</fr:p>
            <fr:p><fr:link type="external" href="https://github.com/dhsorens">GitHub</fr:link> | <fr:link type="external" href="https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4937-6984">ORCID</fr:link> | <fr:link type="external" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/derekhsorensen/">LinkedIn</fr:link></fr:p>
